There was once a seagull who fell in love with the sea.
She'd moistened her legs in the white and salty foam.
She'd fill the sea with presents:
Flowers, garland, shells which she'd dropped from the air in the middle of the waves.
But in the morning the deepest sadness overwhelmed her as she found all of her presents lying all over the sand.
She flew right into the sea filled with pain and rage.
And so she drowned between the waves and her own tears.
